          "text": "Create a 16-bit color pixel image of the eiffel tower as a jpg\n\nDeliver the result as image and/or video files, working in the current directory.\n- Save the finished files in ./output/. Only what is in ./output/ is published as the result.\n- Formats: images as .png, .jpg, .webp, .gif or .svg; videos as .mp4 or .webm. At most 8 files,\n  each under 2 MB; videos at most 10 seconds.\n- Tools available on this machine: python3 3.9.6 (standard library only), node 26.11.1 (no npm packages), ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2. Don't install packages or download anything.\n- Keep any code you write to make the files (it's published as the source), but delete\n  intermediate files such as rendered frames when you're done.\n- Only create or edit files inside the current directory.\n- Finish with a short summary of what you made.\n"
